# TypeScript

- Prefer explicit types on exported functions and shared contracts in `types/`
- Do not use `any` unless bridging untyped Phaser/Colyseus edges — narrow immediately
- Shared client/server shapes live only in `types/` — do not duplicate interfaces
- Prefer `const` enums or string-union message names matching `types/Messages.ts`
- Handle errors; never empty `catch {}`
